.\" -*- coding: UTF-8 -*-
.if \n(.g .ds T< \\FC
.if \n(.g .ds T> \\F[\n[.fam]]
.de URL
\\$2 \(la\\$1\(ra\\$3
..
.if \n(.g .mso www.tmac
.TH lxc-checkpoint 1 2026-08-01 "" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
lxc-checkpoint \- checkpoint a container 
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
'nh
.fi
.ad l
\fBlxc-checkpoint\fR \kx
.if (\nx>(\n(.l/2)) .nr x (\n(.l/5)
'in \n(.iu+\nxu
{-n \fIname\fR} {-D \fIPATH\fR} [-r] [-s] [-v] [-d] [-F]
'in \n(.iu-\nxu
.ad b
'hy
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\fBlxc-checkpoint\fR checkpoints and restores containers.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-r, \-\-restore\fR\*(T> 
Restore the checkpoint for the container, instead of dumping it.
This option is incompatible with \*(T<\fB\-s\fR\*(T>.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-D \fR\*(T>\fIPATH\fR\*(T<\fB, \-\-checkpoint\-dir=\fR\*(T>\fIPATH\fR 
The directory to dump the checkpoint metadata.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-s, \-\-stop\fR\*(T> 
Optionally stop the container after dumping. This option is
incompatible with \*(T<\fB\-r\fR\*(T>.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR\*(T> 
Enable verbose criu logging.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-d, \-\-daemon\fR\*(T> 
Restore the container in the background (this is the default).
Only available when providing \*(T<\fB\-r\fR\*(T>.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-F, \-\-foreground\fR\*(T> 
Restore the container in the foreground. Only available when
providing \*(T<\fB\-r\fR\*(T>.
.SH "COMMON OPTIONS"
These options are common to most of lxc commands.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-?, \-h, \-\-help\fR\*(T>
Print a longer usage message than normal.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-\-usage\fR\*(T>
Give the usage message
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR\*(T>
mute on
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-P, \-\-lxcpath=\fR\*(T>\fIPATH\fR
Use an alternate container path. The default is /var/lib/lxc.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-o, \-\-logfile=\fR\*(T>\fIFILE\fR
Output to an alternate log
\fIFILE\fR. The default is no log.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-l, \-\-logpriority=\fR\*(T>\fILEVEL\fR
Set log priority to
\fILEVEL\fR. The default log
priority is \*(T<ERROR\*(T>. Possible values are :
\*(T<FATAL\*(T>, \*(T<ALERT\*(T>,
\*(T<CRIT\*(T>,
\*(T<WARN\*(T>, \*(T<ERROR\*(T>,
\*(T<NOTICE\*(T>, \*(T<INFO\*(T>,
\*(T<DEBUG\*(T>, \*(T<TRACE\*(T>.

Note that this option is setting the priority of the events
log in the alternate log file. It do not have effect on the
ERROR events log on stderr.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-n, \-\-name=\fR\*(T>\fINAME\fR
Use container identifier \fINAME\fR.
The container identifier format is an alphanumeric string.
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-\-rcfile=\fR\*(T>\fIFILE\fR
Specify the configuration file to configure the virtualization
and isolation functionalities for the container.

This configuration file if present will be used even if there is
already a configuration file present in the previously created
container (via lxc-create).
.TP 
\*(T<\fB\-\-version\fR\*(T>
Show the version number.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.TP 
lxc-checkpoint -n foo -D /tmp/checkpoint
Checkpoint the container foo into the directory /tmp/checkpoint.
.TP 
lxc-checkpoint -r -n foo -D /tmp/checkpoint
Restore the checkpoint from the directory /tmp/checkpoint.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBlxc\fR(7),
\fBlxc-create\fR(1),
\fBlxc-copy\fR(1),
\fBlxc-destroy\fR(1),
\fBlxc-start\fR(1),
\fBlxc-stop\fR(1),
\fBlxc-execute\fR(1),
\fBlxc-console\fR(1),
\fBlxc-monitor\fR(1),
\fBlxc-wait\fR(1),
\fBlxc-cgroup\fR(1),
\fBlxc-ls\fR(1),
\fBlxc-info\fR(1),
\fBlxc-freeze\fR(1),
\fBlxc-unfreeze\fR(1),
\fBlxc-attach\fR(1),
\fBlxc.conf\fR(5)
